 <Note>
   In both OSS SDKs the content is optional: pass only `metadata` and/or an expiration date to update those while keeping the existing content. At least one of the three must be provided, otherwise the call raises.
+</Note>
+
+<Note>
+  In the Python OSS SDK, `updated_at` records the latest memory update, including metadata-only changes that preserve the stored text. It is not the date of the described event and does not establish that a fact is current. For example, adding an audit tag to an older assertion changes `updated_at` without changing that assertion.
 </Note>
 
